## Goal
Flag using a `void` call as a value (`uint64 x = VoidFn();`, or any non-void context).

## Source
tm-editor-plus-plus `src/Components/ItemEditor/IE_GmSurf.as` (2026-09-02). Game compile failed; `openplanet-lsp check` reported 0 errors (24 unrelated warnings).

## Repro
```angelscript
void Dev_FindPatternCached(const string &in pat) {}
void Use() {
    uint64 fn = Dev_FindPatternCached("48 85 C0");
}
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
Components/ItemEditor/IE_GmSurf.as (316, 21) :  ERR : Data type can't be 'void'
```

## LSP today
Silent. `openplanet-lsp check` on the full E++ tree accepted the call site.

## Acceptance
- [ ] `T x = VoidFn();` is an error for any non-void T
- [ ] passing a void call as an argument is an error
- [ ] `VoidFn();` as a statement stays silent
- [ ] Regression fixture

## Notes
Sibling of the definition-site miss: the callee was declared `void` but contained `return PatternCache::Get(pat);` (`Can't return value when return type is 'void'`). Two sites, two engine messages.